  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training - 2018 Healthcare Executive Leadership Training Programs, through Meridian International Center</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding is partially supporting three separate and distinct 14-day training programs to bring approximately 62 Chinese healthcare executives and officials to introduce them to best practices in healthcare management and U.S. advanced medical technologies and solutions. These training programs will also be supported by members of the U.S.-China Healthcare Cooperation Program. This funding in the amount of $67,648.50 is being added to the 2018 Healthcare Executive Leadership Training Programs Reverse Trade Mission Series. This memorandum serves as a no-cost modification to the decision and project memoranda for the 2018 Healthcare Executive Leadership Training Program (USTDA Activity No. 2018-61003A). The change designates the National Healthcare Security Administration as the Chinese partner for the second and third training programs of the reverse trade mission series.</narrative>
  </description>
